{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The parts, the head.</b> The head was not included in the general term of flaying, for it had already been severed at slaughter, and therefore Scripture mentions it separately. And why is the peder mentioned? To tell you that he places the peder with the head and covers with it the place of slaughter. And the word ha-peder is the fat, and so its Aramaic translation is תרבא, and it is called peder — which is the word reversed, as if one said he-ferd — because it separates between the upper innards and the lower ones, and it was a mark of honor on high to spread it over the place of slaughter; and so to this day it is the custom of the nobles of the lands among the nations that they spread it over the roast."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:44.966594973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}